text:
dana: Heads-up from the QA pass on the latency dashboard: the time scrubber isn’t announced by VoiceOver and in compact layout the heatmap bucket context is lost (users can’t tell which percentile band the hover preview belongs to). Screenshot: https://img.redwood/compact-heatmap-qa.png

lucas: Oof. Compact is saving pixels but losing semantics. We should make the scrubber a proper slider and surface a live region for the preview.

priya: For compact buckets we can keep density by hiding the full label but expose an abbreviated label (p50/p95/p99) on focus and via keyboard. Also make each bucket focusable so screen reader users can tab through.

noah: Copy note: the toggle currently reads "Sampling" which people interpret as sampling method. Can we change to "Sampling frequency" or "Sample rate" + a short tooltip?

ivy: Also ran contrast checks: the compact p95 badge fails for small text. a11y tool flagged 3.6:1 on dark mode.

 a11y-bot: Axe report: text in .compact .p95-badge fails contrast (3.6:1). Recommendation: increase fill contrast or add 2px stroke; ensure ratio >= 4.5:1 for normal text.

priya: Example ARIA implementation I suggest:
<pre><code>&lt;div role="slider" tabindex="0" aria-valuemin="0" aria-valuemax="100" aria-valuenow="42" aria-label="Time scrubber: 42%"&gt;
  &lt;span class="handle"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div aria-live="polite" class="sr-only" id="heatmap-preview"&gt;Preview: p95 = 210ms (bucket 4 of 12)&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;!-- heatmap cells: add aria-colindex & role="gridcell" so screen readers read position --&gt;
&lt;div role="gridcell" aria-colindex="4" tabindex="-1"&gt;...&lt;/div&gt;
</code></pre>

lucas: Nice. I’ll wire role="slider" and the aria-live region in the component today. Priya, can you add focus outlines + abbreviated labels for keyboard focus? Noah, can you pick the microcopy variant?

noah: Leaning "Sample rate" (short) and tooltip: "How often we sample traces for heatmap aggregation. Lower = cheaper, noisier." Mobile short: "How often we sample."

ivy: I’ll propose a color tweak: bump the p95 badge fill by 10% darkness and add a 1.5px white inner stroke to keep it legible on both light and dark themes.

dana: Great. Action items: 1) Lucas implement slider + live region (A11Y-411). 2) Priya add focusable gridcells + abbreviated labels in compact mode (DX-668). 3) Noah update the toggle copy and tooltip. 4) Ivy submit color patch and verify contrast. Please link PRs here when ready. Thanks :sparkles:
